# mia-dsv41.env.lowmem-proposal — PROPOSAL ONLY (D-053), not applied anywhere.
#
# Lead's finding 2026-10-16: with V4.1 resident, MemAvailable is ~7.3 GiB on
# gx10-01 and ~5.2 GiB on gx10-02 (MAX_MODEL_LEN=600000, GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.85,
# KV_CACHE_MEMORY_BYTES=2.5 GiB, boot margin 6), below hostwatch CRIT (15).
#
# Can the rollback keep >= 15 GiB per node? No, not by tuning the kit:
#   EXL3 weights alone are 99.5 GiB per rank (kit weight_budget.py). Measured
#   idle MemAvailable with no model: head 106.0-113.7 GiB, worker 115.0-117.2.
#   Best case with ZERO KV and ~2 GiB of CUDA/NCCL overhead:
#     head   113.7 - 99.5 - 2 = 12.2 GiB   (106.0 -> 4.5 GiB)
#     worker 117.2 - 99.5 - 2 = 15.7 GiB
#   vLLM additionally needs KV for one max_model_len sequence, the sparse
#   indexer prefill workspace (scales with max_model_len) and activations, so
#   the head can never reach 15 GiB with V4.1 resident; the worker only with
#   an impractically small window.
#
# The least-bad profile below trades context and concurrency for ~2-3 GiB per
# node (estimate, unmeasured): 600K -> 128K window shrinks the indexer
# workspace, the KV pool drops to 1 GiB, one sequence, and the pool cap
# follows. Expected resident MemAvailable: head ~9-11 GiB, worker ~8-10 GiB.
# It still breaches the 15 GiB floor; the real fix is that V4.1 stays the
# ROLLBACK (only loaded after a failed V4 Flash switch), or a headless head
# node (owner decision, see D-051 open items).
#
# To try it (maintenance window, V4.1 active): merge these lines into
# mia-dsv41/.env, restart V4.1 through the orchestrator, and measure.
MAX_MODEL_LEN=131072
MAX_NUM_SEQS=1
KV_CACHE_MEMORY_BYTES=1073741824
GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.84
MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=1536
DSV41_BOOT_MARGIN_GIB=6
